/**
 * VECTOR Lifescape — School Major Outcomes
 * File: school_major_outcomes.js
 * Version: 1.0 — July 10, 2026
 *
 * PURPOSE:
 * Real, school-specific, per-major outcomes data: program size, median earnings 4 years
 * after completion, and median federal loan debt. Sourced directly from the U.S. Dept of
 * Education College Scorecard Field of Study file (Most-Recent-Cohorts-Field-of-Study.csv),
 * filtered to VECTOR's 282-school universe (union of SCHOOL_ENROLLMENT, UNIVERSITY_CONTENT,
 * and SCHOOL_CULTURE_CATEGORY canonical name sets) and to Bachelor's Degree records only.
 *
 * Master's, doctoral, certificate, and other credential-level records exist in the source
 * file but are intentionally excluded here -- this file is undergraduate-outcomes only.
 * If graduate-level outcomes are ever needed, re-run against the same source file with the
 * CREDDESC filter changed; the source CSV covers all credential levels already.
 *
 * SCHOOL NAME RESOLUTION:
 * School keys use VECTOR canonical names. Naming mismatches between this source file and
 * VECTOR's canonical convention were resolved via VECTOR_NAME_CROSSWALK.js's FOS_ALIAS_MAP
 * before extraction -- see that file for the 13 specific aliases involved.
 *
 * KNOWN GAPS (confirmed genuinely absent from the source file, not a naming issue):
 *   - Deep Springs College (too small to meet federal reporting thresholds)
 *   - Texas A&M University at Galveston (reports under Texas A&M University-College Station)
 *   - University of Montana Western (no field-of-study data found under any name variant)
 *
 * CIP CODE GRANULARITY NOTE:
 * The "cip" field here is 4-digit (e.g. "1107"), matching this source file's own reporting
 * level. This is COARSER than the 6-digit CIP codes used in naics_to_cip_bridge.json and
 * cip_to_naics.json (e.g. "11.0701") -- joining this file to those requires a rollup step
 * (truncate the 6-digit code to its first 4 digits), not a direct string match.
 *
 * DATA QUALITY NOTE:
 * Federal privacy suppression ("PS") and not-applicable ("NA") source values are converted
 * to null here rather than kept as sentinel strings. Roughly half of medianEarnings4yr and
 * medianDebt values are null due to small-cohort suppression -- this is normal Scorecard
 * behavior, not a defect in this file. programSize (enrollment count) is populated for
 * ~95% of records and is the most reliable field for "does this school have a real program
 * here" signal when earnings/debt are null.
 *
 * SCHOOLS: 271 of VECTOR's 282-school universe have at least one Bachelor's-level record
 * (Marion Military Institute is in VECTOR's universe but offers no bachelor's programs,
 * hence no entry here -- correct, not a gap).
 * RECORDS: 16,300 school-major pairs.
 *
 * Source: U.S. Department of Education College Scorecard, Field of Study file,
 * Most-Recent-Cohorts-Field-of-Study.csv, extracted 2026-07-10.
 */

